  "Id": 667,
  "Title": "E-marking begins at Aga Khan University Examination Board",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "AKU-EB examinations are all marked electronically.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p>Following the SSC composite examinations conducted by Aga Khan University Examination Board (AKU-EB) in May 2007 the marking of scripts have begun.</p><p>AKU-EB examinations are all marked electronically. The MCQ papers are marked through the e-Scoring method whereas all CRQs are marked through the e-Marking software.</p><p>A team of over 300 markers and senior markers will be marking the CRQs at two locations, that is, Karachi and Lahore. AKU-EB aims to complete its marking within three weeks.</p><p>Computer-assisted marking not only protects the candidate against marker error but also enables marking to be completed on a timely basis as well as providing valuable analysis of student performance by subject and areas that need improvement.</p><p>The integrity and transparency of its examinations are major priorities for AKU-EB.</p>",
